From 3d5cd6f41cd15564a4580e118deea65f351fc3af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:31:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 37/41] MCP server: fill in documents, screenshots, open
 projects, render lights

- kicad_api completes a request's document specifiers (top level or in an ItemHeader) from the
  open editors: the type from the command's package, the project name and path, the board file
  name.  A common command naming no type goes to each open editor until one handles it.  An
  agent calling GetSchematicNetlist or SaveDocumentToString without a document got a bare
  AS_UNHANDLED (and RevertDocument "the requested project  is not open"); now they work, and
  AS_UNHANDLED says what is missing.
- kicad_screenshot: a PNG of what the app shows, GPU canvases included (TextureView.getBitmap
  on Android, over a Qt grab of the frame and its dialogs).  KIPLATFORM::UI::GrabAppImage();
  only the Qt port implements it.
- kicad_open_project opens a project (file or folder) in the project manager.
- RunBoardJobExportRender keeps the job's default lights and zoom for fields a request leaves
  out; all-zero lights rendered black.
- The instructions mention the above and that open files changed on disk are reloaded.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
